WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:09.425
Jason Obawemimo's site is built like a game console's home screen after hours. His career is the library on it.

2
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:15.617
Every arrival opens on a title screen: his name, over a used car lot at night.

3
00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:20.283
Then, who's playing. Hiring, running a dealership, or just looking.

4
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:25.108
Then a build: pick the role you're hiring for, or the problem on your lot.

5
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:30.317
Sign it and keep it: the card, its link, and a one-page resume for that role.

6
00:00:30.158 --> 00:00:39.608
Then the library: the dealership he runs, the CRM, the voice AI, prospecting, neuroscience, and Obavia, in development.

7
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:45.433
Moving focus crossfades the key art, and brings in that title's layer of the score.

8
00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:51.042
Open a title and it gets its own page: overview, films, trophies, loadout.

9
00:00:50.858 --> 00:01:00.908
In Lead to Title, run the sale desk he built: scan the license once, and every form fills itself. Fictional buyer, example figures.

10
00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:07.717
Each of the 18 trophies is a verified fact. Open every career title for the platinum.

11
00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:14.542
Level 53: one level for each car he has personally sold since June 2025.

12
00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:20.875
Player 2 tunes your build: four proofs, a backdrop, and a finish the library unlocks.

13
00:01:20.708 --> 00:01:25.708
The resume opens as a deck, and Check me opens every proof link.

14
00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:29.833
Every fact stays in plain HTML. Press start.

